    explanation: "This patient has ulcerative colitis (UC), characterized by continuous mucosal inflammation starting at the rectum and extending proximally, with crypt abscesses and pseudopolyps.\n\nExtraintestinal manifestations of UC fall into two categories:\n\nCorrelated with disease activity (improve with treatment):\n• Erythema nodosum (tender red nodules on shins)\n• Peripheral arthritis\n• Episcleritis\n• Oral aphthous ulcers\n\nIndependent of disease activity:\n• Primary sclerosing cholangitis\n• Ankylosing spondylitis\n• Pyoderma gangrenosum (partially independent)\n• Uveitis\n\nErythema nodosum is the most common skin manifestation that correlates with disease activity.",
    educationalObjective: "Erythema nodosum is an extraintestinal manifestation of UC that correlates with disease activity. Other activity-dependent manifestations include peripheral arthritis, episcleritis, and oral ulcers.",
