    stem: "A 7-year-old boy is brought to the physician by his mother because of a 2-day history of high fever and rash. He has also been irritable and refusing to eat. Physical examination shows bilateral non-exudative conjunctivitis, cracked lips, strawberry tongue, cervical lymphadenopathy, and a polymorphous rash on the trunk. Swelling of the hands and feet is noted. Which of the following is the most serious complication of this condition?",
