    explanation: "This patient has Kawasaki disease, an acute vasculitis of medium-sized arteries affecting children, typically under age 5. The most serious complication is coronary artery aneurysms.\n\nDiagnostic criteria (fever ≥5 days plus ≥4 of 5):\n1. Bilateral non-exudative conjunctivitis\n2. Oral mucosal changes (strawberry tongue, cracked lips)\n3. Cervical lymphadenopathy (>1.5 cm)\n4. Polymorphous rash\n5. Extremity changes (edema, erythema, later desquamation)\n\nCoronary artery aneurysms occur in 25% of untreated patients and can lead to:\n• Coronary thrombosis and MI\n• Sudden cardiac death\n• Long-term coronary artery disease\n\nTreatment with IVIG + aspirin within 10 days reduces aneurysm risk to <5%.",
