    stem: "A 70-year-old man comes to the physician because of progressive difficulty urinating for 6 months. He reports weak stream, hesitancy, and nocturia. Digital rectal examination shows a symmetrically enlarged, smooth, and rubbery prostate. Laboratory studies show PSA of 2.5 ng/mL. Which of the following zones of the prostate is most likely affected?",
