    stem: "A 35-year-old man is brought to the emergency department after being found unresponsive. His temperature is 40.2°C (104.4°F), blood pressure is 170/100 mm Hg, and pulse is 130/min. Physical examination shows dilated pupils, diaphoresis, and severe muscle rigidity. He is agitated and confused. His girlfriend reports he takes a medication for depression. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
